---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const records = [
  { number:'01', name:'Architecture breakdown', file:'01-architecture-breakdown.md', question:'What owns what?', content:'UI, persistence and the CSV serializer have explicit responsibilities. A deployment choice remains an open question.' },
  { number:'02', name:'Phased build plan', file:'02-phased-build-plan.md', question:'What becomes useful first?', content:'MVP saves searches. v1 exports them. Collaboration waits for a separate decision. Each phase has an observable finish.' },
  { number:'03', name:'Task backlog', file:'03-task-backlog.md', question:'What work is next?', content:'Priority, phase, owner, estimate and dependencies make the work discussable. Unresolved assignments remain visible.' },
];
---
<div class="ca-blueprint ca-exhibit" data-example="blueprint">
  <p class="ca-kicker">The project before the first feature</p>
  <div class="ca-blueprint-grid">{records.map((record) => <article>
    <span class="ca-blueprint-number" aria-hidden="true">{record.number}</span>
    <h3>{record.name}</h3><p class="ca-connection">{record.question}</p><p>{record.content}</p>
    <a href={`${base}/examples/greenfield/${record.file}`}>Read {record.file}</a>
  </article>)}</div>
  <p class="ca-exhibit-footnote">Illustrative Markdown documents for the same saved-search product. These were authored for explanation, not generated by a completed interview. They retain unresolved decisions deliberately; no approval, initialization, or automatic cross-document synchronization is claimed.</p>
</div>
